Subject: [PATCH 11295/11362] [outer-loop] Append dated corrections to 10
 triaged ledger notes after independent review

An independent reviewer re-derived the load-bearing facts in the 17 notes committed at
81ed76b7cf and refuted numbers in several. This commit APPENDS a dated correction to each
affected Note. No number is silently replaced, no disposition changes, no row is added or
removed. The ledger parses clean (0 malformed) and OPEN stays at 96.

One correction is a category error, not a count error: the `_moat_rigor_claims_null` note
said exp5007 wraps `moat_retired_bounded` and that normalisation was seen unwrapping it.
Nothing was wrapped; the dict a grep matched is the `field_principles` entry. Zero artifacts
wrap the field. WONTFIX survives because the true prevalence points the same way and the
code order holds on reading, not because of the stated verification. The correction says so.

The other corrections are counts with the conclusion intact: exp6275 has 10 zero-CI cells
and 5 crossing zero (not 9 and 6) with a tied best cell; exp5008 carries one corrigendum, not
six (five hits were the lint's own fixture payloads); exp6961's 288 `inference_ran` values
split 216 opportunity rows plus 72 event rows; `beats_vote` is in 17 distinct artifacts, not
19; a top-level `_minus_vote_delta` key is in 8 artifacts, 25 only as a string anywhere; the
capstone-lint citation is lines 258-269, not 265-269; scan population statements added
(7192 parsed, 28 skipped over 20 MB); and the gate-status scan omitted five dict-valued
entries (exp5013 and siblings), harmless but recorded.

Root of every refuted number: a surface scan (string occurrences, a grep, a hand tally of
printed rows). Every number derived by parsing structure agreed. Same defect class the
QA-layer discipline hunts in code, showing up in triage prose.

Residual the reviewer could not close is closed here: the full verifier was run on scratch
COPIES of the seven helper-probed artifacts and the helper-level results reproduce through
the real check sequence; the only writes into the artifact dict are in the stamping path
(adversarial_verify.py lines 7389-7397), never in a check body.

